1. Introduction
   A Perl script that, when supplied three sequences s1, s2, and d 
   in FASTA format, will calculate the LOD for d treating s1 and s2 
   as models like we did in class. The calculation is based upon 
   
     exp( L(Ms1 |d) - L(Ms2 |d))
     
   This script uses find_percent.pl for the probability calulation of
   given model sequences (S1, S2)
   

2. Running Environment
   Tested on windows XP and UNIX with Perl 5.8.0


3. Features
   A. Input File
       a. Each sequence file should be FASTA format and contain
          only one sequence (either DNA or Protein).
          If multiple sequences are found in a single file, 
          only the first sequence will be used for calculation
          
   B. Sequence Check
       a. This script distinguish the input sequence is 
          DNA, protein, or errorneous sequences. This is done by
          checking non DNA character and non amino acid character.           
       b. All the three sequence file (S1, S2, Data) should be 
          either all protein or all DNA. Otherwise, this script 
          will show an error message. 
   
   C. Result File
       a. It will contain a table of probabilities and LOD scores.

   D. Laplace Correction
      To prevent a probability of character to be Zero(o), the laplace
      correction algorithm has been implemented. Depending on the 
      sequence type, one count will be added to all the characters
      including missing ones.       

4. Options
   * Options are case-insensitive and double dash can be used as well
   -s1      :     The first sequence model file (Model1)
   -s2	    :     The second sequence model file (Model2)
   -d       :     The data sequence file to be calculated
   -o       :     To specify the output file. 
                  (This is optional). If not specified, the output file
                  will be DataFileName.LODResult

                  
5. Sample Usages
     >./LOD2.pl -s1 seq1 -s2 seq2 -d seq3
       - Output file is 'seq3.LODResult'

     >./LOD2.pl -s1 seq1 -s2 seq2 -d seq3 -o /tmp/juhur/LODResult.txt
       - Output file will be located at '/tmp/juhur/' with the name 
         as LODResult.txt
         
6. Exception(Error)
   A. when no input sequence file specified
   B. when the specified input file does not exist in the same directory
      (or in the specified directory )
   C. when the specified input file contains errornous sequences
   D. when the three sequences are different types

      
   